  "notes": "Geometric density-peak extraction of filled markers on official Opus 5 launch chart (Frontier-Bench v0.1, internal mini-SWE-agent harness, mean reward over 5 attempts/task; Opus 4.8 served as fallback on safety-classifier refusals for Opus 5/Fable 5 per chart caption). GPT-5.6 Sol series shares its light-gray marker/line color with the chart's vertical gridlines; recovered via density-peak blob detection (gridlines are thin strokes, markers are filled discs) with a widened gray color window ((222,220,210)-(242,240,230)) and a lower min_count (1200) than the tool default (1400) to catch a partially-occluded marker. Opus 4.8 (blue) recovered via a new 'blue' entry added to scripts/digitize_chart.py SERIES_COLORS ((20,95,190)-(70,145,235)), a mechanical extension of the existing color-window pattern (this chart family's Opus 4.8 is drawn blue, unlike the Sonnet 5 pilot's gold Opus 4.8). Score % as-is; convert to 0-1 for catalog scores.",
